---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Hero from '../../../../components/Hero.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import OperatorCard from '../../../../components/OperatorCard.astro';
import FAQSection from '../../../../components/FAQSection.astro';
import { getActivity, getRegion } from '../../../../data/site-data';
import { buildServiceSchema, buildBreadcrumbSchema, buildFAQSchema } from '../../../../data/schema';

const activity = getActivity('snorkeling');
const region = getRegion('miami');

const faqs = [
  {
    question: 'Where is the best snorkeling in Miami?',
    answer: 'Biscayne National Park is the best snorkeling in Miami, it protects 95% underwater park with living coral reefs. Key Biscayne and South Pointe Park are also excellent shore-entry options. For the best experience, take a snorkel tour from Biscayne National Park or Key Largo (30 minutes south).'
  },
  {
    question: 'Do you need a boat for snorkeling in Miami?',
    answer: 'No, there are excellent shore snorkeling spots in Miami. South Pointe Park jetty, Key Biscayne, and Virginia Key all offer shore entry. However, boat tours reach the best reefs in Biscayne National Park and the Florida Keys, which are only accessible by boat.'
  },
  {
    question: 'What is the best time of year for snorkeling in Miami?',
    answer: 'Year-round, but the best conditions are March through June when water temperatures are 75–85°F and seas are calm. Summer (July–September) has the warmest water but higher chance of afternoon storms. Winter water stays around 72–76°F, swimmable with a shorty wetsuit.'
  },
  {
    question: 'How much does snorkeling in Miami cost?',
    answer: 'Shore snorkeling is free at public beaches. Snorkel tours from Biscayne National Park cost $50–$90 per person including gear. Key Largo reef tours run $60–$120. Private charters start around $300 for up to 6 people.'
  },
  {
    question: 'Can beginners snorkel in Miami?',
    answer: 'Absolutely. Biscayne National Park and Key Biscayne have calm, shallow waters perfect for beginners. Many tour operators offer guided snorkeling with instruction and all gear included. South Pointe Park is a popular free beginner spot.'
  }
];

const schema = [
  buildServiceSchema({
    name: 'Snorkeling in Miami',
    description: 'Best snorkeling spots and tours in Miami, Biscayne National Park, Key Biscayne, and more.',
    url: '/florida/miami/snorkeling/',
    areaServed: 'Miami, Florida',
    offers: {
      '@type': 'Offer',
      price: '50',
      priceCurrency: 'USD'
    }
  }),
  buildBreadcrumbSchema([
    { label: 'Home', url: '/' },
    { label: 'Florida', url: '/florida/' },
    { label: 'Miami', url: '/florida/miami/' },
    { label: 'Snorkeling', url: '/florida/miami/snorkeling/' }
  ]),
  buildFAQSchema(faqs)
];
---

<Layout title="Snorkeling in Miami, Best Spots & Tours" description="Discover the best snorkeling in Miami: Biscayne National Park, Key Biscayne, and more. Top spots, tour recommendations, prices, and tips." schema={schema}>
  <Breadcrumbs items={[
    { label: 'Home', url: '/' },
    { label: 'Florida', url: '/florida/' },
    { label: 'Miami', url: '/florida/miami/' },
    { label: 'Snorkeling' }
  ]} />

  <Hero
    title="Snorkeling in Miami"
    subtitle="Miami's best snorkeling is hiding in plain sight, Biscayne National Park protects living coral reefs just 30 minutes from downtown. Here's where to go, what it costs, and how to pick the right tour."
  />

  <!-- Best spots -->
  <section class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-ocean-900 mb-6">Best Snorkeling Spots in Miami</h2>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
      <a href="/florida/miami/biscayne-national-park/snorkeling/" class="group bg-white rounded-xl border border-gray-200 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md transition-all p-6">
        <div class="flex items-start justify-between">
          <div>
            <h3 class="font-bold text-ocean-900 group-hover:text-ocean-600">Biscayne National Park</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mt-1">⭐ Top pick, 3,600 searches/mo</p>
          </div>
          <span class="text-2xl">🐠</span>
        </div>
        <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 mt-3">95% underwater park with living coral reefs, sea turtles, and tropical fish. Boat tours from Homestead or Coconut Grove.</p>
        <span class="inline-flex items-center mt-4 text-sm font-medium text-ocean-600">View guide →</span>
      </a>
      <a href="/florida/miami/key-biscayne/snorkeling/" class="group bg-white rounded-xl border border-gray-200 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md transition-all p-6">
        <div class="flex items-start justify-between">
          <div>
            <h3 class="font-bold text-ocean-900 group-hover:text-ocean-600">Key Biscayne</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mt-1">Best shore entry</p>
          </div>
          <span class="text-2xl">🏝️</span>
        </div>
        <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 mt-3">Calm, shallow waters with seagrass beds and occasional manatees. Free shore access at Crandon Park.</p>
        <span class="inline-flex items-center mt-4 text-sm font-medium text-ocean-600">View guide →</span>
      </a>
      <a href="/florida/miami/south-beach/snorkeling/" class="group bg-white rounded-xl border border-gray-200 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md transition-all p-6">
        <div class="flex items-start justify-between">
          <div>
            <h3 class="font-bold text-ocean-900 group-hover:text-ocean-600">South Pointe Park</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mt-1">Free & easy</p>
          </div>
          <span class="text-2xl">🌊</span>
        </div>
        <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 mt-3">The jetty at South Pointe Park attracts fish and offers easy shore snorkeling right in South Beach.</p>
        <span class="inline-flex items-center mt-4 text-sm font-medium text-ocean-600">View guide →</span>
      </a>
      <a href="/florida/florida-keys/key-largo/snorkeling/" class="group bg-white rounded-xl border border-gray-200 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md transition-all p-6">
        <div class="flex items-start justify-between">
          <div>
            <h3 class="font-bold text-ocean-900 group-hover:text-ocean-600">Key Largo (day trip)</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mt-1">Worth the drive</p>
          </div>
          <span class="text-2xl">🪸</span>
        </div>
        <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 mt-3">John Pennekamp Coral Reef State Park, the only living coral barrier reef in the continental US. 45 minutes from Miami.</p>
        <span class="inline-flex items-center mt-4 text-sm font-medium text-ocean-600">View guide →</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Tour operators -->
  <section class="bg-ocean-50 py-12">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-ocean-900 mb-6">Recommended Snorkeling Tours</h2>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-dashed border-ocean-200 bg-white p-6 text-center col-span-full">
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">Verified tours and operators for this spot are being added. Check back soon, or <a href="/list-your-business/" class="text-ocean-600 underline">list your business</a> if you run one here.</p>
          </div>
      </div>
      <p class="text-xs text-gray-500 mt-4">* Water Fun Club may earn a commission from bookings made through these links. Prices are indicative and may vary.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- What to expect -->
  <section class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-ocean-900 mb-6">What to Expect</h2>
    <div class="prose-custom">
      <h3>Water Conditions</h3>
      <p>Miami's bay waters are generally calm and protected. Visibility ranges from 15–40 feet depending on season and recent weather. Summer offers the clearest water; winter can bring occasional northerly winds that stir up sediment.</p>
      
      <h3>Marine Life</h3>
      <p>You'll see tropical fish (angelfish, parrotfish, grunts), sea turtles, and occasionally manatees in the seagrass beds. Biscayne National Park is home to over 500 species of fish and 30 species of coral.</p>
      
      <h3>Gear</h3>
      <p>Most tours include mask, snorkel, and fins. If you're snorkeling from shore, bring your own gear or rent from local shops ($15–$25/day). A rash guard or shorty wetsuit is recommended November–April.</p>
      
      <h3>Safety</h3>
      <p>Always check conditions before entering the water. Biscayne Bay is generally safe, but heed rip current warnings at ocean beaches. Never touch coral, it's both fragile and protected by law.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- FAQ -->
  <section class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 pb-12">
    <FAQSection items={faqs} />
  </section>
</Layout>